Apple today added the 12-inch MacBook (2017), iPad (6th generation), and BeatsX headphones to the <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102772">obsolete products list</a> on its website.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2022/06/2016-12-inch-macbook-feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-849606" /><br/>
Apple considers a product to be obsolete once seven years have passed since it last distributed the product for sale, including to resellers. <br/>
<br/>
Apple Stores and Apple Authorized Service Providers are instructed to discontinue hardware service for obsolete products and generally cannot order parts for these products as a result. However, Apple says MacBooks may remain eligible for battery replacements for up to 10 years after distribution ended, subject to parts availability.<br/>
<br/>
